# Rust build output, including the generated token crate's.
/target
dist/rust/target/
dist/rust/Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk

# The examples sit outside the workspace on purpose — a consumer is not a
# workspace member — so each builds into a target directory of its own that
# `/target` does not cover. Their lockfiles are kept: they pin nothing but a
# path dependency, and committing them would only produce churn.
/examples/*/target
/examples/*/Cargo.lock

# Docs-site build output. The *sources* (css/, js/, assets/) are committed;
# the rendered site is not — CI builds and deploys it.
/docs-site/public

# Scratch area for hand-vendored inputs (fonts, reference palettes). The folder
# itself is kept so the vendoring workflow in AGENTS.md has somewhere to land;
# nothing inside it is ever tracked.
/.TEMP/*
!/.TEMP/.gitkeep

# NOTE: /dist is deliberately NOT ignored. Generated token artifacts are
# committed so consumers work via submodule, subtree, sparse checkout, raw copy
# or direct URL fetch with no build step. `cargo xtask check` verifies they are
# in sync with the spec.

# The developer's private, machine-specific agent notes. May exist beside any
# AGENTS.md and is never committed. See NOCTUA.md §3.4.
AGENTS.local.md

# `nix build` output symlink.
/result
/result-*
